### 2. Fix the Mini Stepper vs Outer Stepper Logic
The mini stepper in the DataGrid breaks because it relies strictly on findIndex(label === state), whereas the large stepper correctly uses currentOrder. We will align the DataGrid's activeStep calculation so both steppers move perfectly in sync.
**Find the workflowState column in your columns array, and replace its renderCell logic with this:**
```javascript
renderCell: (params) => {
  const state = params.value || "";
  const workflow = params.row.approvalWorkflow;
  const isRejected = state === "REJECTED" || params.row.batchStatus === "R";

  const stepLabels = workflowStepsMap[workflow] || ["Step 1", "Loading..."];
  
  // FIX: Align mini-stepper logic with the big stepper using currentOrder
  let activeStep = params.row.currentOrder ? params.row.currentOrder - 1 : stepLabels.findIndex((label) => label === state);
  
  // Auto-complete timeline if it reaches terminal states
  if (state === "POSTED" || state === "SCHEDULED" || state === "APPROVED" || state === "C" || state === "S") {
    activeStep = stepLabels.length;
  }
  if (activeStep === -1) activeStep = 0;

  const escalationHours = params.row.escalationTime || 24;
  const hoursPending = Math.abs(new Date() - new Date(params.row.requestDate)) / 36e5;
  const isEscalated = !isRejected && activeStep < stepLabels.length && hoursPending > escalationHours;

  return (
    <Box sx={{ width: "100%", display: "flex", alignItems: "center", justifyContent: "flex-start", pl: 2, height: "100%" }}>
      <Stepper activeStep={activeStep} alternativeLabel connector={<CustomConnector />} sx={{ width: "100%", mt: 0.5 }}>
        {stepLabels.map((label, index) => {
          const isCompleted = index < activeStep;
          const isCurrent = index === activeStep;

          let statusFlag = "PENDING";
          if (isCompleted) statusFlag = "COMPLETED";
          if (isCurrent && isRejected) statusFlag = "REJECTED";
          else if (isCurrent && isEscalated) statusFlag = "ESCALATED";
          else if (isCurrent) statusFlag = "ACTIVE";

          return (
            <Tooltip title={label} key={`${label}-${index}`} arrow>
              <Step completed={isCompleted} active={isCurrent} sx={{ px: 0, opacity: isRejected && index > activeStep ? 0.3 : 1 }}>
                <StepLabel
                  StepIconComponent={() => (
                    <CustomWorkflowIcon statusFlag={statusFlag} iconLetter={label.charAt(0).toUpperCase()} label={label} isMini={true} />
                  )}
                  sx={{ p: 0, m: 0 }}
                />
              </Step>
            </Tooltip>
          );
        })}
      </Stepper>
    </Box>
  );
},

```
### 3. Fix the Half-Visible Creator ID
MUI <Chip> components have aggressive truncation properties that cut off the ID if the column width isn't extremely wide. Replacing the Chip with a Flexbox Stack ensures the name truncates cleanly while the ID remains fully visible.
**Find the creatorName column in your columns array, and replace its renderCell with this:**
```javascript
renderCell: (p) => {
  const name = p.row.creatorName || p.row.creatorId;
  const id = p.row.creatorId;
  
  return (
    <Stack direction="row" alignItems="center" spacing={1} sx={{ width: "100%", overflow: "hidden", px: 1 }}>
      <AccountCircleIcon sx={{ color: "text.secondary", fontSize: 20 }} />
      <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ whiteSpace: "nowrap", overflow: "hidden", textOverflow: "ellipsis" }}>
        {name} <strong>({id})</strong>
      </Typography>
    </Stack>
  );
},

```
### 4. Add the Self-Delete Button alongside Proceed/Close
We need to add the Delete button to the sticky bottom Action Bar, visible only if the batch is Pending and created by the current user.
**First, add this Delete API handler to your component (if you don't already have it):**
```javascript
const handleDeleteSelfBatch = async () => {
  setIsSubmitting(true);
  try {
    await callApi(`/JS/voucher/my-requests/by-batch/${viewingBatchId}`, null, "DELETE");
    showSnackBar(`Batch ${viewingBatchId} deleted successfully.`, "success");
    handleCloseViewModal();
  } catch (error) {
    showSnackBar("Failed to delete batch", "error");
  } finally {
    setIsSubmitting(false);
  }
};

```
